            <ArticleTitle>Ruptured splenic abscess presenting as pneumoperitoneum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous pneumoperitoneum follows perforation of hollow viscus; rarely, it may arise from pulmonary interstitial emphysema or intestinal inflammatory disease. We report a 30-year-old man with ruptured splenic abscess who presented with acute abdomen and had pneumoperitoneum. He was treated with splenectomy and is asymptomatic 2 months later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
